/// A value that may or may not be present.
///
/// `T?` is a builtin status type: either a present `T` or the `none` sentinel.
/// There are no `Some`/`None` constructors — bare values auto-wrap to the
/// present branch at return and assignment (type.optionals/OPT5-6). `none` is
/// the absence literal, like `true` and `false`.
///
/// It has **no methods**. The operator surface is the whole API:
///
///     x?              is it there?          [OPT9]
///     x is none       is it absent?         [OPT15]
///     if x? as v      bind the payload      [OPT19]
///     x ?? v          value, or this one    [OPT11]
///     x ?? return e   or leave, saying why
///     try x           or leave as `none`    [type.errors/ER16]
///     x!              or panic              [OPT13]
///     take slot       move it out, leave none [OPT32]
///
/// Each job has one spelling, and the fallbacks are lazy by construction —
/// which is why the eager/lazy method pairs other languages carry aren't here.
public enum Option<T> { }
